// The compiler's streaming trace, reached only through the host. With
// `JET_TRACE_FILE` set the host writes one Chrome trace event per call and
// flushes it, stamping wall time and memory itself (resident and peak
// memory on every `end`; the live heap, `heap_kb`, on a phase's `end`), so a
// running compile can be watched; without it the request carries no sink
// and every call site is one `if trace_sink == .Val(sink)` branch. The
// compiler never formats or buffers events.
//
// `name` is the stable span kind (`load`, `sema.check`, `sema.module`, ...);
// `detail` labels one item (a module or function name, "" for a phase);
// `index`/`total` place the item in its phase (-1 when not counted). `end`
// closes the innermost open span of kind `name`, together with any deeper
// span an early return left open, and reports how many items it processed.
// `progress` reports `done` of `total` items of the open phase; the host
// throttles it. A `progress` kind `counters.<phase>.<counter>` is instead one
// #4319 scaling counter value (`done`), written once. `functions` says whether
// per-function spans were requested (`JET_TRACE_DETAIL=functions`).
pub trait CompilerTraceSink {
    fn begin(self, name: String, detail: String, index: Int, total: Int) Never!
    fn end(self, name: String, items: Int) Never!
    fn progress(self, name: String, done: Int, total: Int) Never!
    fn functions(self) -> Bool Never!
}
